    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14183" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόφαν-σις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποφαίνω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>declaration, statement,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				72a11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1395b6
			</span></i> (as v.l.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἀποφάνσεων περαίνειν τὸ πᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Id.</u>
					2.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Logic,
				<i>predication,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατά τινος</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό τινος,</span>
			<i>affirmative</i> or <i>negative,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Int.</u>
				17a25
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.59
			</span></i>.</div>
